@segment 17-20 Redridge I & Loch Modan II
@start-level 17
# Added 2026-11-11 from the Questie audit (tools/questie_near.py): 161 A Dark Threat Looms (1350 XP) is taken and carried to Dun Modr, where segment 12 goes anyway.
# Skyborne Druid 17-20 (the Dwarf route's segment 05, adapted).
# Carry-in: 65 (to Wiley in Lakeshire), 263 (Stonesplinter troggs), 353 (package for Mountaineer Stormpike),
# 2039 (Find Bingles).
# Carry-out: 119 + 121 (Lakeshire, segment 07), 455 (Menethil Harbor, segment 08), 2041 (Stormwind, segment 07).
# Hearth: Sentinel Hill at the start (not used), Thelsamar from the Loch Modan part on. It is used once, at the
# very end, to come back from Moonglade.
# Deviations from the Dwarf original:
#  - The whole level-20 water class-quest chain of the Dwarf is gone (94494 from Ironforge, Norric Lochthane, 94495, 94497 and 94499 at
#    Hervdana Saegrund's cave in the Wetlands). Travel removed with it: the walk through the Dun Algaz tunnels
#    out into the Wetlands and east along the cliffs to Hervdana's falls (nothing else was done there), and the
#    stop at Norric's house. Travel KEPT because other quests use it: the second Ironforge trip (301/302 for
#    Prospector Stormpike, 2041 from Gnoarn) and the run north to the Dun Algaz tunnel (468 to Mountaineer
#    Rockgar, 455 Dragonmaw at the Loch Modan end of the tunnels).
#  - The first Ironforge trip (tram from Stormwind) existed only to train at level 18: it is removed. You train
#    at Sheldras Moontree in the Stormwind Park instead and take the gryphon from Stormwind to Thelsamar.
#  - Level 20 training: the Dwarf trained in Ironforge. Here it is a Teleport: Moonglade trip (Loganaar) at
#    the very end of the segment, from the Dun Algaz tunnel. The Hearthstone has not been used in this segment
#    up to that point, and the Dwarf route hearthed to Thelsamar at this same moment, so the way back is the
#    same Hearthstone use.
#  - The L 20 grind step is gone: it only made sure that class quest could be taken in Ironforge.
#  - Cat Form is NOT learned here: its chain starts in Darnassus and is done in the Darkshore segment. An N
#    step at the Moonglade stop says so.
#  - Combat hints rewritten for a druid without Cat Form (caster form, Bear Form, Bash, Entangling Roots,
#    Hibernate from 18).
# Left out on purpose: 132 (Wiley's follow-up, a Westfall bounce), 161/274 (A Dark Threat Looms part 3 and 4: the
# data puts Ashlan Stonesmirk at Dun Modr in the far north of the Wetlands, not at the dam), 278 and
# 255/256/271/531 (elite), 116 Dry Times (four bought drinks from four towns).
@carry 65,263,353,2039,93963,97894
@done 237,1097

# ---------- Stormwind -> Redridge ----------
A 244 | From the Dwarven District leave Stormwind by the main gate and follow the road east: Goldshire, Eastvale Logging Camp, then the Three Corners crossroads just inside Redridge. Guard Parker walks the road there.
F Lakeshire @ Redridge Mountains, 25.5, 59.4 | Follow the road north-east to Lakeshire. Ariena Stormfeather, the gryphon master, stands on the south side of the bridge. Redridge Mongrels (15-16) and Great Goretusks sit next to the road: leave them for now.
T 244 | Deputy Feldon, a few steps from the gryphon master
A 246 | Deputy Feldon
A 98407 @ Redridge Mountains, 25.6, 59.9 | Deputy Feldon: Show of Force (new in Forever)
A 3741 | Shawn, a child standing at the lake by the bridge (24.2, 53.6)
A 125 | Cross the bridge. Foreman Oslow stands at its north end.
A 118 | Verner Osgood, close to the bridge on the town side
A 120 | Magistrate Solomon in the town hall
A 127 | Dockmaster Baren on the dock in front of the town
A 129 | Darcy, the waitress in the inn
T 65 | Wiley the Black, upstairs in the inn. Do not take his follow-up (The Defias Brotherhood, back to Westfall).
A 92 | Chef Breanna, in the house west of the inn

# ---------- Lake Everstill ----------
C 3741 | Glinting Mud lies under water along the lake shore on both sides of the bridge (spots between 14 and 33, 51-56). Open the piles until one holds Hilary's Necklace.
C 125 @ Redridge Mountains, 36.4, 54.7 | Swim east from the bridge. The Sunken Chest with Oslow's Toolbox lies on the lake bottom. Murlocs (17-20) swim around it: kill what comes at you before you dive, and keep the fish they drop (Spotted Sunfish for Selling Fish).
T 3741 | Hilary, the girl next to Shawn
T 125 | Foreman Oslow
A 89 | Foreman Oslow

# ---------- Gnolls north of town ----------
C 89 @ Redridge Mountains, 24.0, 34.8 | The data lists the gnolls north of Lakeshire as the source of Iron Pikes and Iron Rivets: Redridge Brutes (17-18) in the camps around 24, 35 and Redridge Mystics (18-19) a little further north. Take the path north out of town. Pull one camp member at a time with Wrath, stun a Mystic's cast with Bash in Bear Form, and hold a second gnoll in Entangling Roots if two come. Do not go deeper than you need: Bashers (19-20) are behind them. Great Goretusks on the way drop snouts for the goulash.

# ---------- Gnolls and beasts south of the lake ----------
C 246,98407 @ Redridge Mountains, 20.0, 70.0 | Cross the bridge again and work the gnoll camps south and south-west of Lakeshire, toward Three Corners. Kill 10 Redridge Mongrels (15-16) and 6 Redridge Poachers (16-17, mostly in the southern camps around 29, 80), and every Redridge Thrasher (14-15) you see until you have 5 Spiked Collars. Poachers shoot: run up to them. Moonfire a gnoll that runs at low health. Tarantulas (15-16) and Great Goretusks (16-17) live between the camps: kill them as you go for 5 Crisp Spider Meat and 5 Great Goretusk Snouts (Redridge Goulash).
T 129 | Guard Parker at Three Corners
A 130 | Guard Parker
C 127 @ Redridge Mountains, 43.7, 69.2 | 10 Spotted Sunfish from murlocs. Murloc Shorestrikers (16-17) on the south shore of the lake around 44, 69 are the easiest; Minor Tidecallers and Flesheaters (17-19) live further along the shore and in the water. This is a level 21 quest: pull single murlocs from the edge of a camp, stun the Tidecallers' heals with Bash in Bear Form and finish runners with Moonfire, because they run and bring friends. Keep every Murloc Fin you loot: Dockmaster Baren asks for 8 of them in the next segment. The condors for the goulash are next.
C 92 @ Redridge Mountains, 47.7, 56.9 | Redridge Goulash: the 5 Tough Condor Meat come from Dire Condors (18-19), which fly over the hills south and east of the lake, close to the murloc shore. Fight them one at a time with full health. If you still miss Crisp Spider Meat or Goretusk Snouts, Tarantulas and Great Goretusks are around Three Corners and all along the road back to Lakeshire.

# ---------- Lakeshire hand-ins ----------
T 246 | Deputy Feldon
T 98407 @ Redridge Mountains, 25.6, 59.9 | Deputy Feldon
T 89 | Foreman Oslow, north end of the bridge
T 127 | Dockmaster Baren
T 130 | Martie Jainrose, the herbalist on the west side of town
A 131 | Martie Jainrose
T 92 | Chef Breanna
T 131 | Darcy in the inn

# ---------- Stormwind and Goldshire ----------
FLY Stormwind | Ariena Stormfeather, south of the bridge
T 120 | From the gryphon master walk through the Trade District to the Valley of Heroes, the bridge inside the main gate. General Marcus Jonathan sits on his horse there.
A 121 | General Marcus Jonathan. Keep it: you are back in Lakeshire in the next segment.
T 118 | Walk out of the gate and down the road to Goldshire (two minutes). Smith Argus works in the smithy.
A 119 | Smith Argus. Keep the Crate of Horseshoes for the next segment.
TRAIN @ Stormwind City, 35.8, 67.4 | Walk back into Stormwind. Sheldras Moontree, the druid trainer in the Park on the west side: learn your level 18 spells (Hibernate puts a beast to sleep, Faerie Fire). If he offers a druid quest you have not seen yet, take it.
FLY Thelsamar | Dungar Longdrink, the gryphon master in the Trade District. If he does not offer Thelsamar, take the Deeprun Tram from the Dwarven District to Ironforge and fly from Gryth Thurden there.
S Thelsamar | Innkeeper Hearthstove in the Stoutlager Inn. Buy food and water here.

# ---------- Loch Modan: the southern troggs ----------
A 436 | Jern Hornhelm in Thelsamar (37.2, 47.4)
C 263 @ Loch Modan, 33.0, 80.0 | Follow the road south past the Valley of Kings tower and turn east into the Stonesplinter Valley. Kill what is still missing of 10 Stonesplinter Shamans and 10 Bonesnappers (15-16). Stun a Stonesplinter Shaman's cast with Bash in Bear Form.
T 263 | Mountaineer Wallbang in the southern guard tower
A 217 | Captain Rugelfuss, in the same tower
A 86585 | Back in the Stonesplinter Valley: the body of Mountaineer Ylva lies at 31.7, 86.4 (new in Forever)
C 86585 | Use the Banner of Ironforge next to the body. The trogg Headsplitter comes for it: kill him. Clear the troggs around the spot first so nothing joins the fight.
C 217 | Grawmug (17) and his guards Gnasher and Brawler (16) stand together in the cave at the very back of the valley (34.8, 90.5). Clear the cave on the way in. Then fight in Bear Form with Demoralizing Roar up, kill the two guards first and Grawmug last, and Bash one of them to get a heal off when you drop below half.
T 217 | Captain Rugelfuss
T 86585 | Captain Rugelfuss

# ---------- The north: Stormpike and the dam ----------
T 353 | Run the road north through Thelsamar to the northern guard tower. Mountaineer Stormpike is in the tower (24.8, 18.4).
A 250 | Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII, in the middle of the Stonewrought Dam at the north end of the loch
T 250 | Walk east along the dam and down the eastern ramp. The Suspicious Barrel stands at 56.1, 13.2 with two Dark Iron Sappers (17) next to it: kill them one after the other.
A 199 | From the Suspicious Barrel
T 199 | Back to Chief Engineer Hinderweir.
A 161 | Chief Engineer Hinderweir: A Dark Threat Looms. The powder goes to Dun Modr in the north of the Wetlands. Do not go now: the route is there at level 30 (segment 12), keep it in your log until then

# ---------- East shore and the Farstrider Lodge ----------
T 2039 | Go back down the eastern ramp and follow the east shore of the loch south. Bingles Blastenheimer stands by his broken flying machine. Stay on the shore: the Mo'grosh ogres in the hills north-east of the loch are elite.
A 2038 | Bingles Blastenheimer. You collect his tools after the lodge.
A 385 | Keep south-east to the Farstrider Lodge. Marek Ironheart is inside.
A 86758 @ Loch Modan, 81.8, 61.6 | Marek Ironheart: Twisting the Knife (new in Forever)
A 257 | Daryl the Youngling, in the lodge. This starts a 15 minute timer.
C 257 | Kill 6 Mountain Buzzards (15-16). They fly over the hills right outside the lodge, south and west of it.
T 257 | Daryl the Youngling
A 258 | Daryl the Youngling. A 12 minute timer: no detours.
C 258 | Kill 5 Elder Mountain Boars (16-17). They roam north-west of the lodge, on the slopes toward Bingles (around 66, 40). Run straight there, kill five and run straight back.
T 258 | Daryl the Youngling
C 385,86758 @ Loch Modan, 61.9, 44.7 | Go back to the east shore. Loch Crocolisks (14-15) lie along the shore and in the shallows from Bingles north: kill them for 5 Crocolisk Meat and 6 Crocolisk Skins. Daggerfang, the crocolisk for Marek's knife, hunts along the same shore (seen between 59 and 66, 34-55). Hibernate puts a second crocolisk to sleep. Do not touch the Large Loch Crocolisk (22 elite).
C 2038 @ Loch Modan, 51.0, 25.0 | Swim out to the islands in the north of the loch. Three toolbuckets hold the Wrench (48.7, 30.1), the Screwdriver (48.4, 20.5) and the Hammer (51.8, 24.1); the Blastencapper lies at 54.2, 26.6. Crocolisks swim between the islands.
T 2038 | Back to Bingles Blastenheimer on the east shore
T 385 | Marek Ironheart at the Farstrider Lodge
T 86758 @ Loch Modan, 81.8, 61.6 | Marek Ironheart

# ---------- Ironband's Excavation Site ----------
T 436 | The dig is south-west of the lodge. Magmar Fellhew stands in the camp above it.
A 297 | Magmar Fellhew
A 298 | Prospector Ironband, next to him. Just a letter for Thelsamar.
A 86613 @ Loch Modan, 70.2, 64.5 | Excavation Tools (new in Forever). The quest starts from the Excavation Tools you pick up inside the dig; the data has no exact spots. Look for tool sets on the ground while you kill troggs, and pick up six. If you find none, press Skip here and on its hand-in.
C 297,86613 @ Loch Modan, 70.2, 64.5 | Go down into the dig. Stonesplinter Geomancers (17-18), Diggers (18-19) and Berserk Troggs (19-20) drop the 8 Carved Stone Idols. Stun the Geomancers' fire spells with Bash in Bear Form, pull from the edge and hold a second trogg in Entangling Roots. Collect the six tool sets while you are down there.
T 297 | Magmar Fellhew
T 86613 @ Loch Modan, 65.9, 65.6 | Prospector Ironband

# ---------- West shore and Thelsamar ----------
A 86614 | Walk west along the south end of the loch and up its west shore. The Discarded Fishing Toolbox lies on the shore at 48.8, 54.0 (new in Forever).
T 86614 | Khara Deepwater, the fishing trainer on the shore north-east of Thelsamar (40.4, 39.4)
T 298 | Jern Hornhelm in Thelsamar
A 301 | Jern Hornhelm

# ---------- Ironforge: Prospector Stormpike and Gnoarn ----------
FLY Ironforge | Thorgrum Borrelson in Thelsamar
T 301 | Prospector Stormpike in the Hall of Explorers
A 302 @ Ironforge, 74.6, 11.7 | Prospector Stormpike
A 2041 | Gnoarn the gnome (ForeverChanges shows him at 62.2, 29.2; Questie has him in Tinker Town at 69.2, 50.6). A letter for Stormwind, handed in in the next segment.

# ---------- Loch Modan: the shipment ----------
FLY Thelsamar | Gryth Thurden
T 302 | Jern Hornhelm
A 273 | Jern Hornhelm
A 468 | Mountaineer Kadrell walks the road through Thelsamar (needs level 19)
T 273 | Huldar waits on the road south of the loch (52.2, 69.3), on the way to the dig
A 454 | Huldar
T 454 | Miran, next to him
A 309 | Miran. This starts an escort to the excavation site.
C 309 @ Loch Modan, 52.2, 69.4 | Walk with Miran. Dark Iron dwarves ambush the cart on the way: let them come to you, fight in Bear Form and kill them one at a time; Entangling Roots holds a second one. Miran must survive.
T 309 | Prospector Ironband at the excavation camp

# ---------- Dun Algaz ----------
T 468 | Walk back around the south end of the loch, through Thelsamar and up the road north. Mountaineer Rockgar guards the Dun Algaz tunnel in the north-west corner of Loch Modan (25.4, 10.4)
A 455 | Mountaineer Rockgar
C 455 | Follow the road into the Dun Algaz tunnels. Dragonmaw Scouts (19-20) and Grunts (20-21) stand along the road and in the side camps: kill 8 Scouts and 6 Grunts, as far as you get without going out into the Wetlands. They hit hard for your level: one at a time, Bear Form when they reach you, Moonfire the ones that run, heal between pulls. Whatever is missing you can finish in segment 08.

# ---------- Moonglade: level 20 training ----------
N Cast Teleport: Moonglade | Right where you stand, when you have had enough of the Dragonmaw. Your Hearthstone has not been used in this segment, so it is ready to bring you back to Thelsamar.
TRAIN @ Moonglade, 52.5, 40.6 | Loganaar, the druid trainer in Nighthaven: learn everything up to your level (level 20 brings Starfire). Still 19? Take what he has; the rest comes at the next trainer.
N Cat Form comes later @ Moonglade, 52.5, 40.6 | Cat Form is a quest chain that starts with the druid trainer in Darnassus at level 20. This route does it in the Darkshore segment (about level 24-25), so there is nothing to do for it here. If Sheldras Moontree in Stormwind offers "The Great Cat Spirit" when you next stand in front of him, take it.
H Thelsamar | Hearthstone back to the inn
